      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "CHANG Tsung-yüan 章宗源 (T. 逢之), 1752?–1800, scholar, was a native of Shan-yin, Chekiang, and a distant relative of Chang Hsüeh-ch'êng [q. v.]. His family, once well-to-do, met reverses of fortune during his grandfather's time, chiefly owing to a disastrous tidal wave.",
          "source": "eccp-3633303",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
          "text": "章宗源，字逢之。",
